1
00:01:21,999 --> 00:01:26,337
<i>Sharkboy was not always
half-shark, half-boy.</i>

2
00:01:26,547 --> 00:01:30,676
<i>He was a marine biologist,
or at least in training.</i>

3
00:01:31,217 --> 00:01:33,512
<i>His father studied
great white sharks...</i>

4
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,889
<i>...and called his son "Sharkboy"...</i>

5
00:01:36,097 --> 00:01:38,892
<i>...because of how much he loved
to care for sharks.</i>

6
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:43,146
<i>He made them sushi
and had given them all names.</i>

7
00:01:43,354 --> 00:01:49,486
<i>Good Milk, Piggy,
Egg Battle and Kraken.</i>

8
00:01:53,699 --> 00:01:58,035
<i>But one day, an incredible,
mysterious storm appeared.</i>

9
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:01,038
<i>It swept away the entire laboratory.</i>

10
00:02:01,247 --> 00:02:03,750
-Sharkboy!
<i>-Thanks to the life rafts...</i>

11
00:02:03,958 --> 00:02:06,419
-<i>...Sharkboy and his father survived.</i>
-Sharkboy!

12
00:02:06,628 --> 00:02:09,255
<i>But they survived on
different sides of the wreckage...</i>

13
00:02:09,465 --> 00:02:11,717
<i>...each floating off
in a different direction.</i>

14
00:02:11,925 --> 00:02:13,092
Sharkboy!

15
00:02:13,301 --> 00:02:16,971
<i>Sharkboy was completely alone.</i>

16
00:02:18,765 --> 00:02:21,643
<i>Almost completely.</i>

17
00:02:21,894 --> 00:02:24,979
<i>But one of the sharks
recognized him.</i>

18
00:02:25,481 --> 00:02:26,940
Hey. It's Sharkboy.

19
00:02:27,148 --> 00:02:30,652
Don't take a bite out of him, boys.
He's a friend.

20
00:02:31,570 --> 00:02:37,158
<i>They took Sharkboy to their cave
home, where he'd be safe and dry.</i>

21
00:02:40,537 --> 00:02:43,998
<i>His new family were sharks.</i>

22
00:02:46,334 --> 00:02:49,671
<i>Hundreds of sharks.</i>

23
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:56,762
<i>The sharks raised him
as one of their own...</i>

24
00:02:56,970 --> 00:02:59,848
<i>...training him in the ways
of the shark.</i>

25
00:03:00,056 --> 00:03:02,475
You must keep moving to survive.

26
00:03:02,684 --> 00:03:05,478
Always go forward, never back.

27
00:03:06,437 --> 00:03:10,066
<i>To live by instinct,
and instinct alone.</i>

28
00:03:14,153 --> 00:03:18,784
<i>Eventually, he grew gills
and sharp talons for claws.</i>

29
00:03:18,992 --> 00:03:21,745
<i>His teeth sharpened
themselves to a point.</i>

30
00:03:22,286 --> 00:03:26,875
<i>He grew fins. All sorts of fins.</i>

31
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:28,919
<i>But that was years ago.</i>

32
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:33,297
<i>I first met Sharkboy while
fishing on a dock this summer.</i>

33
00:03:44,225 --> 00:03:46,477
<i>He seemed lost.</i>

34
00:03:46,687 --> 00:03:49,230
-You have to get a real job.
-No, I have a job.

35
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:50,983
<i>So I snuck him home...</i>

36
00:03:51,315 --> 00:03:54,443
-I can't stand the writing process.
-Maybe you should leave.

37
00:03:54,653 --> 00:03:57,906
<i>...when my parents were
too busy to notice.</i>

38
00:03:59,992 --> 00:04:03,369
<i>I kept him fed and in water.</i>

39
00:04:04,078 --> 00:04:08,457
<i>He had been traveling the universe
in search of his father.</i>

40
00:04:08,667 --> 00:04:12,754
<i>He told me of his latest adventures
on a planet so cool...</i>

41
00:04:12,963 --> 00:04:15,131
<i>...it makes you drool.</i>

42
00:04:15,423 --> 00:04:18,551
<i>He said I, too, could go to
Planet Drool someday.</i>

43
00:04:20,804 --> 00:04:24,766
<i>Then one night,
I was visited by a glowing light.</i>

44
00:04:24,975 --> 00:04:27,894
<i>An amazing girl
with purple flames for hair...</i>

45
00:04:28,102 --> 00:04:30,479
<i>...and skin of molten lava rock
appeared.</i>

46
00:04:30,689 --> 00:04:33,984
<i>I called her Lavagirl.</i>

47
00:04:34,191 --> 00:04:37,613
<i>She smiled at me,
for that seemed to be her name.</i>

48
00:04:37,821 --> 00:04:41,783
<i>She told me she needed Sharkboy
to return to Planet Drool with her...</i>

49
00:04:41,992 --> 00:04:44,410
<i>...for a great crisis was developing.</i>

50
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,705
<i>She asked if I could go with them.</i>

51
00:04:46,913 --> 00:04:49,833
<i>I told her, "I have school tomorrow."</i>

52
00:04:50,042 --> 00:04:53,544
<i>She gave me a sad look
and flamed away...</i>

53
00:04:53,754 --> 00:04:56,213
<i>...taking Sharkboy with her.</i>

54
00:04:57,633 --> 00:05:01,594
<i>I haven't seen Sharkboy
or Lavagirl since then.</i>

55
00:05:03,304 --> 00:05:05,807
And that's what I did this summer.

56
00:05:10,103 --> 00:05:11,897
Enough.

57
00:05:12,313 --> 00:05:15,651
Someone is picking that up.
And it's not gonna be me.

58
00:05:17,778 --> 00:05:21,238
We were supposed to tell
true stories.

59
00:05:21,447 --> 00:05:23,282
That is a true story.

60
00:05:23,659 --> 00:05:27,161
-Does Lavagirl have special powers?
-There's no such thing as Lavagirl.

61
00:05:28,997 --> 00:05:30,247
She can--

62
00:05:33,292 --> 00:05:37,881
-She can shoot lava out of her hands.
-Cool.

63
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:40,717
How many people think
Max's story is true?

64
00:05:41,384 --> 00:05:43,469
-Not true.
-Made-up.

65
00:05:43,679 --> 00:05:46,514
-Not true.
-It's just a made-up story.

66
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:50,018
If it's true,
why don't you bring Sharkboy...

67
00:05:50,226 --> 00:05:52,938
-...and Lavagirl to class tomorrow?
-They went away.

68
00:05:53,146 --> 00:05:55,899
-I don't know where they went.
-Have a seat, Max.

69
00:05:56,108 --> 00:05:58,359
Linus, you're next.

70
00:06:04,866 --> 00:06:06,993
This summer, I met a new friend...

71
00:06:07,201 --> 00:06:09,830
...who was half-dork, half-boy.

72
00:06:10,038 --> 00:06:12,206
I called him Dorkboy.

73
00:06:13,541 --> 00:06:14,876
His real name was Max.

74
00:06:15,085 --> 00:06:20,799
We had him for dinner, but he stunk
so bad that we all blew chunks.

75
00:06:22,383 --> 00:06:23,592
That's enough, Linus.

76
00:06:25,469 --> 00:06:28,681
Linus, Max, stay.

77
00:06:28,890 --> 00:06:32,435
-Come on, Mr. E.
-Class, what's my name?

78
00:06:32,643 --> 00:06:35,688
Mr. Electricidad.

79
00:06:35,897 --> 00:06:38,357
Mr. Electricidad, exactly.

80
00:06:38,566 --> 00:06:43,780
Not "Mr. Electric."
Not "Mr. Electrici...."

81
00:06:44,823 --> 00:06:49,326
Linus, you just earned a minus
for your behavior today.

82
00:06:49,535 --> 00:06:53,206
This is a new year.
Do you think you can be friends?

83
00:06:53,749 --> 00:06:54,958
-No.
-No.

84
00:06:55,167 --> 00:06:57,919
Then it's decided,
you'll be the best of friends.

85
00:06:58,128 --> 00:07:02,423
Which means no more
picking on Max, Linus.

86
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:06,803
Max, you're in the fourth grade.

87
00:07:07,012 --> 00:07:08,679
There are good kids
in this class.

88
00:07:08,889 --> 00:07:12,308
Find them, make friends with them.

89
00:07:12,558 --> 00:07:17,230
Dreaming keeps you from seeing
what's right here in front of you.

90
00:07:17,605 --> 00:07:22,152
This isn't a dream.
This is the real world.

91
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:29,700
-I lost my train of thought.
-No dreaming. Got it.

92
00:07:29,910 --> 00:07:33,621
-I'll try harder.
-What do you have there?

93
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:38,794
It's my dream journal.

94
00:07:39,502 --> 00:07:42,005
It has all of my most
precious dreams in it.

95
00:07:42,214 --> 00:07:45,466
And I'll never part with it
for as long as I live.

96
00:07:46,885 --> 00:07:48,344
You're a good kid, Max.

97
00:07:56,812 --> 00:07:58,521
Max.

98
00:07:58,814 --> 00:08:01,774
Let's be imaginary friends.

99
00:08:01,983 --> 00:08:06,320
You can try and hang with us,
and we'll pretend you don't exist.

100
00:08:06,988 --> 00:08:10,867
Check it out. Sharkboy gets shocked
by electric eels...

101
00:08:11,076 --> 00:08:14,204
...and then they feed
on his cooked flesh.

102
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:16,372
Wow, Linus.

103
00:08:16,747 --> 00:08:19,583
Your skills are weak.

104
00:08:29,343 --> 00:08:32,305
I'm gonna burst your bubble,
dream boy.

105
00:08:35,851 --> 00:08:37,643
You're dead.

106
00:08:37,853 --> 00:08:40,021
Get the book!

107
00:08:51,324 --> 00:08:52,575
Give me the book.

108
00:08:53,243 --> 00:08:57,289
Hand over the book,
or you'll visit the dream world.

109
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:22,230
All right. We got it.

110
00:09:24,690 --> 00:09:27,818
I'll bring you a revised
edition tomorrow.

111
00:09:45,128 --> 00:09:48,298
<i>-Max, wake up.
-Dream, Max.</i>

112
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:52,093
<i>-Open your eyes, Max.
-Eyes open and dream.</i>

113
00:09:52,302 --> 00:09:55,263
<i>-Stay dreaming.
-Wake up!</i>

114
00:10:31,174 --> 00:10:33,467
Sharkboy...

115
00:10:34,468 --> 00:10:36,679
...and Lavagirl.

116
00:10:43,477 --> 00:10:44,980
Max?

117
00:10:45,271 --> 00:10:47,773
My cookies. My giant cookies.

118
00:10:47,983 --> 00:10:50,235
What are you doing baking sweets?

119
00:10:50,484 --> 00:10:52,320
You know what happens
when he eats sugar.

120
00:10:52,528 --> 00:10:54,406
I baked them for his class.

121
00:10:54,613 --> 00:10:57,908
So you could make friends at school,
and now you've eaten them.

122
00:10:58,118 --> 00:10:59,827
No. It was Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

123
00:11:00,286 --> 00:11:04,498
Look. This one has shark bites,
and this one is singed.

124
00:11:04,707 --> 00:11:07,377
There's no such thing
as Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

125
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:08,836
Well, I believe him.

126
00:11:10,504 --> 00:11:11,839
Your mother's right.

127
00:11:12,048 --> 00:11:14,883
When you go to sleep and close
your eyes, they may come back.

128
00:11:15,093 --> 00:11:18,512
When you open them again,
Sharkgirl and Lavaboy will be:

129
00:11:18,721 --> 00:11:20,723
-Out of here.
-But--

130
00:11:20,931 --> 00:11:22,891
Mouth closed. Eyes closed.

131
00:11:23,101 --> 00:11:24,518
-Now?
-Yes, now.

132
00:11:29,982 --> 00:11:32,526
You can wait till you're
in bed to close your eyes.

133
00:11:36,072 --> 00:11:38,866
Kids need their dreams.

134
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:43,329
Kids need to grow up.

135
00:11:48,709 --> 00:11:51,879
He's not making any friends
with these cookies.

136
00:11:55,258 --> 00:11:58,552
There's no such thing
as Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

137
00:11:58,886 --> 00:12:02,556
There's no such thing
as Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

138
00:12:02,931 --> 00:12:04,892
Yes, there is.

139
00:12:06,186 --> 00:12:08,729
Stupid plugs.

140
00:12:09,147 --> 00:12:12,150
Please don't let me
have to go to school.

141
00:12:12,358 --> 00:12:14,985
They'll make fun of me. I know it.

142
00:12:15,278 --> 00:12:20,325
I wish I could just escape this
loser world and go to Planet Drool.

143
00:12:20,533 --> 00:12:24,245
Games and toys
and laughs and fun.

144
00:12:27,290 --> 00:12:29,708
May there be terrible storms...

145
00:12:29,917 --> 00:12:35,215
...rain, sleet, snow, tornados...

146
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:39,094
...so I can lay here
all day tomorrow...

147
00:12:39,302 --> 00:12:42,263
...and dream of Drool.

148
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:10,291
Guess I didn't dream hard enough.

149
00:13:10,916 --> 00:13:14,086
There are good opportunities
out there. You just need to look.

150
00:13:14,295 --> 00:13:17,423
Traffic engineer.

151
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:21,261
Hey.

152
00:13:21,469 --> 00:13:23,929
I was cleaning out my closet,
look what I found.

153
00:13:24,139 --> 00:13:27,267
Remember Tobor,
the robot you tried to build?

154
00:13:27,475 --> 00:13:29,935
Why were you cleaning out
your closet?

155
00:13:30,145 --> 00:13:32,230
I had to find one of these.

156
00:13:32,646 --> 00:13:36,276
-Is Mom making you get a real job?
-Writing is a real job.

157
00:13:38,403 --> 00:13:41,156
-When it pays.
-I'm walking you to school today.

158
00:13:41,364 --> 00:13:45,326
So, what do you say?
Wanna finish making Tobor?

159
00:13:46,452 --> 00:13:49,121
-It won't work.
-Well, how do you know?

160
00:13:49,330 --> 00:13:50,914
Because you told me it wouldn't.

161
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,544
I did?

162
00:13:57,045 --> 00:13:58,839
I'm sorry.

163
00:13:59,715 --> 00:14:04,761
-I should've never said that.
-It's okay. You were right.

164
00:14:05,638 --> 00:14:07,515
Dumb idea.

165
00:14:10,518 --> 00:14:12,604
How did this happen?

166
00:14:13,229 --> 00:14:15,440
The grass was dead anyway.

167
00:14:15,648 --> 00:14:17,733
Why are you so morbid?

168
00:14:18,025 --> 00:14:22,405
I just wish anything could happen so
I wouldn't have to go to school today.

169
00:14:22,614 --> 00:14:25,283
That's not realistic, Max.

170
00:14:25,491 --> 00:14:29,412
It's bad enough your father's head is
in the clouds, but not you too. Okay?

171
00:14:29,621 --> 00:14:32,956
Just push that dream aside
and move on.

172
00:14:33,165 --> 00:14:34,917
Like with your dream?

173
00:14:35,125 --> 00:14:38,504
The one about you and Dad
and me?

174
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:40,506
Well, I do have a dream about us...

175
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:44,843
...but as I'm sure you've been noticing
lately, your father and I are just....

176
00:14:45,052 --> 00:14:46,803
Well, we're...

177
00:14:47,763 --> 00:14:49,224
...not compatible.

178
00:14:49,432 --> 00:14:54,186
Sorry, I don't mean to dump this on
you right before you go to school, but--

179
00:14:54,395 --> 00:14:55,979
School's waiting.

180
00:14:56,188 --> 00:14:58,524
Did we have to move so close
to school?

181
00:14:58,732 --> 00:15:01,527
Your father thought
we'd save money on gas.

182
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:03,404
Come right home
after school today...

183
00:15:03,613 --> 00:15:06,865
...because there's some things
we need to talk about.

184
00:15:07,074 --> 00:15:08,742
I love you.

185
00:15:10,703 --> 00:15:14,748
I wish anything could happen so
I wouldn't have to come home today.

186
00:15:17,418 --> 00:15:20,045
Hey, look. It's dream boy.

187
00:15:25,468 --> 00:15:27,720
Who knows where
tornados come from?

188
00:15:29,763 --> 00:15:34,226
Well, when cold air mixes with
hot air, it can form a tornado.

189
00:15:34,435 --> 00:15:38,063
As the hot and cold chase each other
around and around and around.

190
00:15:38,273 --> 00:15:41,900
I dreamt of a story kind of like
Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

191
00:15:42,109 --> 00:15:43,736
Ice Girl and Dream Boy.

192
00:15:43,944 --> 00:15:46,281
Her powers come from
her Crystal Heart.

193
00:15:47,906 --> 00:15:51,034
-No more fairy tales.
-Piranha Girl and Beluga Boy.

194
00:15:52,035 --> 00:15:53,621
Plastic Boy and Metal Girl.

195
00:15:54,664 --> 00:15:56,291
Barf Boy and Vomit Girl.

196
00:15:56,499 --> 00:15:59,419
Does everyone hear me?
I'm a teacher, right?

197
00:15:59,627 --> 00:16:02,087
Wrong. I'm an awakener.

198
00:16:02,297 --> 00:16:07,050
Only I'm finding it more and more
difficult to keep my class awake.

199
00:16:07,884 --> 00:16:10,638
No recess again for you,
Marissa. Too many allergies.

200
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:13,516
Got more boogers on your homework
than there is homework.

201
00:16:13,725 --> 00:16:16,226
I'm just cold.

202
00:16:16,436 --> 00:16:18,812
I'll be happy to change places
with you.

203
00:16:19,021 --> 00:16:23,401
-It's a lot warmer back in my spot.
-But I have to sit up front.

204
00:16:23,651 --> 00:16:26,153
It's just that you're sitting
right under the vent.

205
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:30,783
-And it's August and you're sneezing.
-You're gonna get me in trouble.

206
00:16:30,991 --> 00:16:32,452
Max.

207
00:16:34,161 --> 00:16:37,122
Are you trying to make real friends?

208
00:16:37,332 --> 00:16:39,417
Yeah. Trying like you told me to.

209
00:16:39,625 --> 00:16:41,084
That's good.

210
00:16:41,293 --> 00:16:43,253
Just not with my daughter, okay?

211
00:16:45,590 --> 00:16:49,885
-No. It wasn't like that. It's just--
-Sit down, Max.

212
00:17:00,896 --> 00:17:04,066
-Give me back my journal.
-Class has begun. Everyone, sit.

213
00:17:04,316 --> 00:17:07,319
-Linus took my journal.
-I did not.

214
00:17:07,528 --> 00:17:10,155
Minus. I mean Linus.

215
00:17:10,365 --> 00:17:13,409
You get a minus for misconduct.
Give Max back his journal.

216
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:19,665
One more time, Linus, and we'll have
to change your name to "Minus."

217
00:17:27,632 --> 00:17:30,843
-He ruined my dream journal!
-I did not.

218
00:17:31,051 --> 00:17:33,513
Mr. Electric, send him
to the principal's office...

219
00:17:33,721 --> 00:17:35,138
...and have him expelled!

220
00:17:36,098 --> 00:17:38,975
You're in my class,
not the other way around.

221
00:17:39,184 --> 00:17:43,021
I know everything,
and you know nothing.

222
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:47,984
At the end of class, both of you will
report to the principal's office...

223
00:17:48,276 --> 00:17:49,779
...with your parents.

224
00:18:13,009 --> 00:18:14,762
Everybody down!

225
00:18:28,526 --> 00:18:30,445
It's them.

226
00:18:40,455 --> 00:18:42,874
I'm looking for Max.

227
00:18:52,925 --> 00:18:54,469
She's hot.

228
00:19:00,056 --> 00:19:03,268
We need your help, Max.
Come with us.

229
00:19:05,521 --> 00:19:07,105
What do I have to do?

230
00:19:07,314 --> 00:19:09,942
Go with us to Planet Drool.
We'll explain on the way.

231
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:12,778
We're going to Planet Drool?

232
00:19:17,324 --> 00:19:19,869
It's my home planet,
just outside our solar system.

233
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:23,831
You should know, Max.
You made it up.

234
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:29,461
-I can't go with you.
-Why not?

235
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:34,341
Because you're not real.
Both of you are just a dream.

236
00:19:35,258 --> 00:19:37,637
And when I open my eyes...

237
00:19:38,011 --> 00:19:39,262
...you'll be gone.

238
00:19:45,018 --> 00:19:46,269
We're still here, Max.

239
00:19:47,354 --> 00:19:51,651
If you wanna stop the Darkness
from destroying our worlds...

240
00:19:51,859 --> 00:19:53,109
...come with us.

241
00:19:54,027 --> 00:19:55,947
You better go with them.

242
00:19:58,281 --> 00:19:59,700
Okay.

243
00:20:00,158 --> 00:20:01,536
I'll go.

244
00:20:04,914 --> 00:20:08,124
Everyone follow me.
We're gonna go find shelter.

245
00:20:08,333 --> 00:20:11,003
I can't believe I'm finally getting
to ditch this place...

246
00:20:11,211 --> 00:20:13,213
...and go to Planet Drool.

247
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:16,049
How are we getting there?

248
00:20:26,936 --> 00:20:29,021
Put these on, everybody.

249
00:20:29,229 --> 00:20:33,025
Blue goggles for the boys,
pink for the girls.

250
00:20:33,525 --> 00:20:35,653
Do you have another pair
of boy goggles?

251
00:20:41,157 --> 00:20:43,744
So how do you fly it?

252
00:20:43,953 --> 00:20:45,078
You don't know?

253
00:20:46,413 --> 00:20:48,624
That's sort of been
the whole problem.

254
00:20:50,250 --> 00:20:51,919
You press "Go."

255
00:21:10,730 --> 00:21:15,026
-Now how do you fly it?
-It's got an autopilot.

256
00:21:15,233 --> 00:21:17,360
You thought of everything,
didn't you, Max?

257
00:21:17,987 --> 00:21:19,989
Not exactly.

258
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:25,452
-How do we land it?
-That's the part I never thought of.

259
00:21:25,661 --> 00:21:29,040
Jupiter, Saturn, Neptune.

260
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:31,249
You might wanna hold on
to something.

261
00:21:53,648 --> 00:21:57,985
-Recognize your dream world, Max?
-Not really.

262
00:21:58,778 --> 00:22:02,322
I feel like I should,
but I just don't.

263
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,700
It's affecting him too.

264
00:22:04,950 --> 00:22:06,952
I thought he would just remember.

265
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:11,916
-Remember what?
-Your dreams. This planet?

266
00:22:12,124 --> 00:22:13,625
Us.

267
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:16,419
Your powers.

268
00:22:16,796 --> 00:22:20,382
-I have powers?
-More than any of us.

269
00:22:20,590 --> 00:22:22,634
Don't you know that?

270
00:22:22,968 --> 00:22:27,347
Everything that is or was
began with a dream.

271
00:22:27,555 --> 00:22:29,474
And you dreamt us, Max.

272
00:22:29,684 --> 00:22:33,145
-Us and this whole place.
-I did?

273
00:22:33,353 --> 00:22:37,315
Every dream you ever had
landed right here on Planet Drool.

274
00:22:37,524 --> 00:22:41,486
-Why is it so dark?
-The planet is dying.

275
00:22:41,696 --> 00:22:43,238
It began yesterday.

276
00:22:43,446 --> 00:22:45,032
What's the calculation, Sharkboy?

277
00:22:47,325 --> 00:22:51,204
Forty-five minutes till the Darkness
destroys Planet Drool.

278
00:22:51,413 --> 00:22:54,083
We didn't go to Earth
to save you, Max.

279
00:22:54,290 --> 00:22:57,044
We need you to save Planet Drool.

280
00:22:58,796 --> 00:23:00,338
But how?

281
00:23:00,547 --> 00:23:03,258
The Dream Lair is on
the other side of the planet.

282
00:23:03,466 --> 00:23:05,301
That's where your dreams
are going bad.

283
00:23:05,510 --> 00:23:07,179
We have to go there and reverse it.

284
00:23:07,387 --> 00:23:09,556
We have to travel through
the Passage of Time...

285
00:23:09,765 --> 00:23:12,935
...catch the Train of Thought, swim
down the Stream of Consciousness...

286
00:23:13,144 --> 00:23:17,106
...and skate across the Sea of
Confusion, now covered in ice.

287
00:23:17,605 --> 00:23:21,568
Why'd you do that, Max?
Why'd you freeze the ocean?

288
00:23:23,653 --> 00:23:27,615
Max didn't mean to do it.
Did you, Max? Max is a good boy.

289
00:23:27,825 --> 00:23:31,286
Otherwise, you and I would be evil,
and we're not evil.

290
00:23:31,578 --> 00:23:33,956
I'm not evil, am I, Max?

291
00:23:34,165 --> 00:23:35,875
I don't-- I don't think so.

292
00:23:36,083 --> 00:23:39,252
That's why we brought you here.
To put things back in order.

293
00:23:39,461 --> 00:23:42,923
We just have to stay positive.
It's not the end of the world.

294
00:23:43,132 --> 00:23:45,176
Not yet, it's not.

295
00:23:47,594 --> 00:23:50,638
The Darkness. Run!

296
00:23:51,431 --> 00:23:53,017
This is like a bad dream.

297
00:23:53,225 --> 00:23:55,978
Oh, yeah? Just wait till you meet
Mr. Electric.

298
00:23:56,187 --> 00:23:58,189
He's the worst bad dream yet.

299
00:24:09,574 --> 00:24:11,827
Where is everyone?

300
00:24:12,036 --> 00:24:15,371
-They're trapped on Mount Neverest.
-By Mr. Electric.

301
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:19,459
But Planet Drool is a place for kids
to dream and have endless fun.

302
00:24:20,836 --> 00:24:22,754
It's endless fun, all right.

303
00:24:22,963 --> 00:24:24,464
Once you get on...

304
00:24:28,301 --> 00:24:29,677
...you can't get off.

305
00:24:29,887 --> 00:24:33,598
Kids aren't allowed to rest,
because if they rest, they sleep.

306
00:24:33,808 --> 00:24:36,768
And if they sleep, they dream,
and if they dream--

307
00:24:36,977 --> 00:24:39,021
It takes power away
from Mr. Electric.

308
00:24:39,230 --> 00:24:41,816
But we're gonna stop him
with our secret weapon.

309
00:24:42,233 --> 00:24:44,985
Shouldn't we save those kids first?

310
00:25:01,168 --> 00:25:03,670
Why can't I do that?

311
00:25:17,226 --> 00:25:19,727
Lavagirl!

312
00:25:37,704 --> 00:25:40,707
Who knows where
Mr. Electric is hiding?

313
00:25:42,709 --> 00:25:44,128
Everyone?

314
00:25:44,669 --> 00:25:48,966
They're not raising their hands.
You're all upside down.

315
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:57,308
<i>Who is stopping my unstoppable
coasters?</i>

316
00:25:59,143 --> 00:26:01,728
<i>-Back in your seats.</i>
-Go. Run. Hide!

317
00:26:01,937 --> 00:26:04,480
-Let's get out of here.
<i>-Everyone back in your seats.</i>

318
00:26:04,899 --> 00:26:06,482
Who's Mr. Electric?

319
00:26:06,691 --> 00:26:09,194
He's supposed to provide light
to the planet...

320
00:26:09,402 --> 00:26:12,323
...but all he brings now is Darkness.

321
00:26:12,990 --> 00:26:14,909
<i>The fun has begun.</i>

322
00:26:31,926 --> 00:26:33,843
He's taking us up.

323
00:26:40,184 --> 00:26:43,895
My home. At half its normal power.

324
00:26:51,778 --> 00:26:54,114
He's taking us down.

325
00:27:00,287 --> 00:27:02,164
Showtime.

326
00:27:17,054 --> 00:27:19,223
Keep playing. Never stop.

327
00:27:19,431 --> 00:27:22,309
Games and toys and laughs--
Hey. Hey.

328
00:27:22,517 --> 00:27:23,935
Hey. Hey. And fun.

329
00:27:28,315 --> 00:27:32,568
Well, well, well.
If it isn't Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

330
00:27:32,777 --> 00:27:35,822
What are you doing halting
my endless fun-coaster...

331
00:27:36,031 --> 00:27:39,159
...and infiltrating my lair?

332
00:27:39,368 --> 00:27:41,412
We don't need permission from you.

333
00:27:41,619 --> 00:27:43,038
Fiery.

334
00:27:43,247 --> 00:27:47,583
I don't believe we've met.
I'm Mr. Electric.

335
00:27:47,792 --> 00:27:49,919
Why are you bringing misery
to our planet?

336
00:27:50,129 --> 00:27:53,298
-You're supposed to be running it.
-"You're supposed to be running it."

337
00:27:53,506 --> 00:27:57,052
I am running it.
Right into the ground.

338
00:27:57,261 --> 00:27:59,804
-Those are my orders.
-Who ordered that?

339
00:28:00,014 --> 00:28:01,889
No school, no discipline, no rules.

340
00:28:02,099 --> 00:28:04,976
And most important, no dreams.

341
00:28:05,185 --> 00:28:09,064
Dreams can destroy you, can't they?
My instincts tell me that is so.

342
00:28:09,273 --> 00:28:12,484
-Oh, really?
-That's why we have to stop you.

343
00:28:12,692 --> 00:28:16,447
You and what army?

344
00:28:21,784 --> 00:28:24,246
-Now?
-Now.

345
00:29:08,956 --> 00:29:10,417
Feel the burn.

346
00:29:16,798 --> 00:29:18,674
Now for reals.

347
00:29:55,254 --> 00:29:58,631
Internal radar, shark-like reflexes.
You're amazing.

348
00:29:58,840 --> 00:30:01,801
But is it enough to defeat
Mr. Electric?

349
00:30:02,093 --> 00:30:04,179
We have our secret weapon.
Remember?

350
00:30:06,639 --> 00:30:11,145
Did you really believe
you could stop me?

351
00:30:12,271 --> 00:30:15,440
I know we can't, but he can.

352
00:30:15,648 --> 00:30:17,650
Take it away, Max.

353
00:30:22,029 --> 00:30:23,698
Show him what you're made of, Max.

354
00:30:23,906 --> 00:30:25,409
What am I supposed to do?

355
00:30:27,076 --> 00:30:30,372
-I told you this would happen.
-I thought he would just remember.

356
00:30:30,581 --> 00:30:32,374
Remember what?

357
00:30:33,417 --> 00:30:35,751
The dream. Remember the dream.

358
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:38,838
I don't remember half my dreams.

359
00:30:40,257 --> 00:30:42,884
That's why I write them
in my dream journal.

360
00:30:46,721 --> 00:30:49,807
What half of your dreams
do you remember?

361
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:51,809
This part I remember.

362
00:30:52,018 --> 00:30:55,897
-Where are you taking us?
-Where all the useless dreams go.

363
00:30:56,105 --> 00:30:58,525
To the Dream Graveyard.

364
00:31:15,875 --> 00:31:19,671
Well, at least we're on
the Passage of Time.

365
00:31:20,087 --> 00:31:24,301
-Maybe it'll take us to the Dream Lair.
-It's going in the wrong direction.

366
00:31:24,509 --> 00:31:26,678
The Dream Lair's that way.

367
00:31:27,762 --> 00:31:29,598
What's in the Dream Lair?

368
00:31:29,805 --> 00:31:32,601
It's where all the dreams
that fuel Planet Drool are stored.

369
00:31:32,808 --> 00:31:34,603
But they're being destroyed.

370
00:31:34,810 --> 00:31:37,397
-How?
-That's what we have to find out.

371
00:31:37,606 --> 00:31:40,983
Soon even Sharkboy
and I will cease to exist.

372
00:31:41,192 --> 00:31:42,611
Duck.

373
00:31:46,531 --> 00:31:49,992
Max, where is your dream journal?

374
00:31:50,201 --> 00:31:51,827
Great thinking, Sharkie.

375
00:31:52,036 --> 00:31:53,746
We can read his dreams out loud...

376
00:31:53,955 --> 00:31:56,207
...and turn everything back
to the way it was.

377
00:31:56,416 --> 00:31:59,711
I may even realize my true identity.

378
00:32:00,002 --> 00:32:01,921
I threw it away.

379
00:32:03,423 --> 00:32:05,800
My journal's back on Earth.

380
00:32:10,555 --> 00:32:12,724
We really thought you were
the answer, Max.

381
00:32:12,932 --> 00:32:14,393
Don't listen to him.

382
00:32:14,601 --> 00:32:18,062
He's upset because you didn't show
up and make him King of the Ocean...

383
00:32:18,272 --> 00:32:20,565
...with a giant fish army
to back him up.

384
00:32:20,773 --> 00:32:22,108
Look who's talking.

385
00:32:22,317 --> 00:32:25,612
You thought you'd find a great use
for your powers and heal the planet.

386
00:32:25,820 --> 00:32:28,532
Max thought his dream world
would be a happy place.

387
00:32:28,948 --> 00:32:31,075
We've all been duped.

388
00:32:41,127 --> 00:32:43,547
I think you broke my fin.

389
00:32:45,299 --> 00:32:46,799
Sorry.

390
00:32:51,012 --> 00:32:53,973
Hey, you. I see you hiding.

391
00:32:54,181 --> 00:32:55,726
Come back here.

392
00:32:57,018 --> 00:32:58,645
I was awakened.

393
00:33:00,146 --> 00:33:01,398
I'm sorry.

394
00:33:01,648 --> 00:33:05,026
Did all the children
from Mount Neverest escape?

395
00:33:05,234 --> 00:33:08,530
With Sharkboy and Lavagirl.
But I took care of it. See?

396
00:33:08,739 --> 00:33:10,449
Someone was with them?

397
00:33:10,657 --> 00:33:13,744
Just another child afraid of his
own shadow. No threat to us.

398
00:33:13,951 --> 00:33:16,705
I banished him
to the Dream Graveyard.

399
00:33:16,912 --> 00:33:20,249
Where old dreams lie?
He could find an ally.

400
00:33:20,459 --> 00:33:23,378
I told you, every dream
must be smashed...

401
00:33:23,587 --> 00:33:25,921
...every child captured.

402
00:33:26,130 --> 00:33:29,468
If you want him back, I'll simply
track him when he falls asleep.

403
00:33:29,676 --> 00:33:32,970
Fool. He's the Daydreamer...

404
00:33:33,179 --> 00:33:37,642
...and the moment he realizes it
will be the moment of our doom.

405
00:33:37,850 --> 00:33:39,226
Now what do you want me to do?

406
00:33:39,436 --> 00:33:42,313
Bring me the boy before
he discovers his true powers...

407
00:33:42,522 --> 00:33:45,149
...and tears my new kingdom apart.

408
00:33:46,150 --> 00:33:49,278
Plugs, redirect the Darkness.

409
00:33:49,696 --> 00:33:51,238
And...

410
00:33:54,283 --> 00:33:57,746
...bring me the Plug Hounds.

411
00:34:04,877 --> 00:34:07,839
We'll never find our way
out of this graveyard.

412
00:34:08,047 --> 00:34:10,759
Darkness headed this way.

413
00:34:12,343 --> 00:34:13,553
Sit down, Max.

414
00:34:13,762 --> 00:34:16,263
-What for?
-Close your eyes and dream.

415
00:34:16,473 --> 00:34:20,059
If Max can't remember his dreams,
maybe he can re-dream them.

416
00:34:20,519 --> 00:34:24,188
-He could dream us out of here.
-Dream, Max.

417
00:34:26,733 --> 00:34:29,235
Now, what do you see?

418
00:34:29,444 --> 00:34:32,739
I see a giant...

419
00:34:32,947 --> 00:34:35,867
...chocolate-chunk
marshmallow cookie...

420
00:34:36,075 --> 00:34:38,578
...with lots of warm milk.

421
00:34:40,329 --> 00:34:43,625
-Sorry, I'm starving.
-Here's some food.

422
00:34:43,834 --> 00:34:47,754
-You're not gonna like that.
-I'm so hungry, I could eat lava rocks.

423
00:34:54,469 --> 00:34:57,304
-What is that?
-Lava rocks.

424
00:34:57,514 --> 00:35:00,307
Here, have some real food.
Fresh sushi.

425
00:35:00,517 --> 00:35:03,437
-It'll knock you right out.
-That's not fresh.

426
00:35:03,645 --> 00:35:06,857
-I'm not sure that's sushi anymore.
-Just a few weeks old.

427
00:35:07,064 --> 00:35:09,443
I'll cook it for you.

428
00:35:13,780 --> 00:35:15,990
That's okay.
I'm not that hungry anymore.

429
00:35:16,198 --> 00:35:19,160
Let me just rest a moment.
Maybe I can sleep.

430
00:35:21,580 --> 00:35:23,956
It's getting closer.

431
00:35:27,293 --> 00:35:29,003
Get out of here.

432
00:35:32,674 --> 00:35:35,342
Max, I know you got
a lot to figure out...

433
00:35:35,552 --> 00:35:40,474
...but if you happen to dream about
who I am and how I fit into this world...

434
00:35:40,682 --> 00:35:43,477
-...it would be helpful for me to know.
-No distractions.

435
00:35:43,685 --> 00:35:46,563
You steer him off-course,
we could be lost in a sea of dreams.

436
00:35:46,813 --> 00:35:49,816
-I'm sorry. I'm desperate.
-Focus on the problem at hand.

437
00:35:50,024 --> 00:35:53,319
Max needs to dream us out of here,
so how about I put him to sleep now?

438
00:35:53,528 --> 00:35:57,239
-No, Sharkboy.
-One punch, he'll be out like a light.

439
00:36:01,035 --> 00:36:05,540
I've seen this before.
It's on the tip of my finger.

440
00:36:06,207 --> 00:36:08,167
It's a hand.

441
00:36:09,794 --> 00:36:11,838
It is a hand.

442
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:14,925
A hand?

443
00:36:15,884 --> 00:36:17,802
Another hand.

444
00:36:18,010 --> 00:36:21,180
-Yep, it's Tobor!
-Who?

445
00:36:21,388 --> 00:36:24,350
Tobor. I dreamt him up
when I was a kid.

446
00:36:24,559 --> 00:36:27,353
A robot that could help me
with my homework.

447
00:36:27,854 --> 00:36:29,731
I tried to build him once.

448
00:36:29,940 --> 00:36:32,651
Everyone kept telling me
he would never work.

449
00:36:32,859 --> 00:36:34,318
So here he is.

450
00:36:34,528 --> 00:36:36,780
A forgotten dream
in the Dream Graveyard.

451
00:36:36,988 --> 00:36:42,076
-Maybe he can help us.
-He's supposed to be very smart.

452
00:36:42,284 --> 00:36:46,581
-Tobor, awake.
-Yes?

453
00:36:46,957 --> 00:36:48,542
He works.

454
00:36:48,750 --> 00:36:50,251
We could ask him anything now.

455
00:36:50,459 --> 00:36:53,630
Let me. Let me.
Tell me something about me.

456
00:36:53,838 --> 00:36:59,218
-I'm clueless.
-Actually, you are extremely bright.

457
00:37:00,845 --> 00:37:05,224
-Am I King of the Ocean, or what?
-No, sorry.

458
00:37:06,350 --> 00:37:08,728
How do I save Planet Drool?

459
00:37:09,395 --> 00:37:12,566
The answer is in your dreams.

460
00:37:13,232 --> 00:37:16,527
You mean if I put him to sleep,
he'll dream us out of this mess?

461
00:37:16,736 --> 00:37:20,447
No. At least not here.

462
00:37:20,657 --> 00:37:23,117
Darkness is falling.

463
00:37:23,325 --> 00:37:25,870
Any dream of his
will become a nightmare...

464
00:37:26,078 --> 00:37:29,290
...and you don't want those
becoming a reality.

465
00:37:29,498 --> 00:37:32,836
But if you go to
the Land of Milk and Cookies...

466
00:37:33,044 --> 00:37:36,715
-Of course.
-...that's where the good dreams are.

467
00:37:36,923 --> 00:37:40,719
-Where the answers are.
-It's perfect, Max.

468
00:37:40,927 --> 00:37:44,346
The Land of Milk and Cookies
is a safe, sweet place.

469
00:37:44,555 --> 00:37:46,850
You'll be able to dream easily there.

470
00:37:47,058 --> 00:37:52,104
-Can you take us?
-I have no body. I can't move.

471
00:37:52,313 --> 00:37:55,066
You can move your eyes
and your mouth.

472
00:37:56,442 --> 00:37:59,153
Why didn't you work
back on Earth, Tobor?

473
00:37:59,361 --> 00:38:02,406
Some dreams are so powerful
they become real...

474
00:38:02,616 --> 00:38:04,659
...like Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

475
00:38:04,868 --> 00:38:09,538
I, on the other hand,
am still only a dream.

476
00:38:10,999 --> 00:38:14,836
-What's wrong?
-Train of thought, I'm losing it.

477
00:38:15,045 --> 00:38:17,797
You were taking us to the Land
of Milk and Cookies, remember?

478
00:38:18,006 --> 00:38:21,092
I mean, I'm literally losing
the Train of Thought.

479
00:38:21,300 --> 00:38:24,595
-It's down there.
-That's the Train of Thought?

480
00:38:24,804 --> 00:38:28,223
-How do I keep it on track?
-With your mind.

481
00:38:28,432 --> 00:38:31,102
The Train of Thought
gets easily distracted.

482
00:38:31,310 --> 00:38:34,105
Stay focused,
and it'll speed you directly...

483
00:38:34,313 --> 00:38:38,442
...to the Land of Milk and Cookies.
The rest is up to you.

484
00:38:38,652 --> 00:38:40,654
Sorry I forgot about you, Tobor.

485
00:38:40,862 --> 00:38:45,992
Are you kidding? You just saved me.
I'm free!

486
00:38:51,748 --> 00:38:54,125
Max, get down here!

487
00:38:56,920 --> 00:39:00,297
-What's wrong?
-We can't control it.

488
00:39:00,506 --> 00:39:02,341
All you have to do is keep it
on track.

489
00:39:02,549 --> 00:39:06,178
How can we keep it on track
if there is no track?

490
00:39:09,640 --> 00:39:12,102
Looks like another dream gone bad.

491
00:39:13,770 --> 00:39:18,565
-What do we do?
-Yell. Scream.

492
00:39:26,741 --> 00:39:29,035
Jump! It'll be all right.

493
00:39:45,426 --> 00:39:49,304
What does it mean when
your Train of Thought wrecks?

494
00:39:49,513 --> 00:39:50,932
Well...

495
00:39:52,224 --> 00:39:53,434
...can't be good, buddy.

496
00:39:53,642 --> 00:39:56,228
How much time do we have,
Sharkboy?

497
00:39:57,814 --> 00:39:59,983
Twenty minutes.

498
00:40:07,406 --> 00:40:09,200
Stick to rotten fish, please.

499
00:40:10,284 --> 00:40:14,080
Chocolate. I stepped in chocolate.

500
00:40:17,499 --> 00:40:19,293
We're here.

501
00:40:24,758 --> 00:40:27,551
The Land of Milk and Cookies.

502
00:40:34,768 --> 00:40:36,770
The milk is warm.

503
00:40:36,978 --> 00:40:39,396
-He'll be out in no time.
-Lay down.

504
00:40:39,605 --> 00:40:42,066
Here's a marshmallow pillow.

505
00:40:42,274 --> 00:40:44,944
How about dreaming us
into the Dream Lair?

506
00:40:47,197 --> 00:40:49,656
The ground is thumping too much.

507
00:40:50,532 --> 00:40:52,786
My highly trained ears hear it too.

508
00:40:53,077 --> 00:40:54,829
Boom, boom, boom.

509
00:40:55,412 --> 00:40:57,498
-Let me hear it.
-I wouldn't.

510
00:41:01,085 --> 00:41:02,294
Hothead.

511
00:41:02,503 --> 00:41:05,297
When you dreamt up
these giant cookies...

512
00:41:05,506 --> 00:41:08,467
...who did you expect
to be able to eat them?

513
00:41:08,675 --> 00:41:10,261
I really didn't think about it.

514
00:41:10,469 --> 00:41:12,638
Because if you dream
giant cookies...

515
00:41:12,847 --> 00:41:16,142
...something has to be created
to consume giant cookies.

516
00:41:24,691 --> 00:41:26,568
Cookie giants!

517
00:41:58,600 --> 00:42:00,602
Frosting.

518
00:42:04,107 --> 00:42:06,817
Those giants almost
looked like my parents.

519
00:42:07,026 --> 00:42:09,736
They seem happy together.
Is that your dream?

520
00:42:09,946 --> 00:42:13,950
We had a dream of family.
It hasn't been coming true lately.

521
00:42:14,158 --> 00:42:16,410
Most dreams don't come true
on their own.

522
00:42:16,618 --> 00:42:18,745
You have to make them true.

523
00:42:18,955 --> 00:42:22,208
Takes a lot of work. Not easy.

524
00:42:22,876 --> 00:42:25,128
But not impossible either.

525
00:42:27,171 --> 00:42:31,633
Stinking fresh air.
Blinding sunlight.

526
00:42:32,218 --> 00:42:37,223
Oh, how I long for
a sky with fluorescent lights.

527
00:42:52,654 --> 00:42:54,615
Stand back.

528
00:42:57,243 --> 00:42:59,536
All right, that one was me.

529
00:43:00,495 --> 00:43:02,831
Still empty-handed, I see.

530
00:43:03,041 --> 00:43:06,002
-You're so powerful, you find him.
-That's your job.

531
00:43:06,210 --> 00:43:08,712
Do it, or I'll have you discharged.

532
00:43:11,257 --> 00:43:13,550
Someone is dreaming in here.

533
00:43:16,095 --> 00:43:20,515
All right, Max. You've had your
cookies and milk, now go to sleep.

534
00:43:20,724 --> 00:43:22,559
I'll try.

535
00:43:23,186 --> 00:43:28,191
-Go to sleep.
-Not like that. Sing him a lullaby.

536
00:43:29,150 --> 00:43:34,238
<i>Dream, dream, dream, dream</i>

537
00:43:35,239 --> 00:43:36,865
Your turn.

538
00:43:37,532 --> 00:43:41,412
<i>Close your eyes, shut your mouth
Dream a dream and get us out</i>

539
00:43:41,620 --> 00:43:44,706
<i>Dream, dream, dream,
Dream, dream, dream</i>

540
00:43:44,915 --> 00:43:48,877
<i>Hit the hay, fast asleep
Dream a dream, you little bleep</i>

541
00:43:49,087 --> 00:43:52,298
<i>Dream, dream, dream,
Dream, dream, dream</i>

542
00:43:57,428 --> 00:43:59,973
It's working!
Keep it up, Sharkboy!

543
00:44:02,016 --> 00:44:05,727
<i>Just relax, lay about
Or my fist will put you out</i>

544
00:44:05,936 --> 00:44:09,232
<i>Dream, dream, dream,
Dream, dream, dream</i>

545
00:44:09,440 --> 00:44:13,319
<i>Take your time, but beware
There is Darkness in the air</i>

546
00:44:13,527 --> 00:44:16,738
<i>Dream, dream, dream
Dream, dream, dream</i>

547
00:44:16,947 --> 00:44:20,951
Dream about me next, Max.
I need to know who I am.

548
00:44:21,702 --> 00:44:25,289
Not just destruction
or a simple flame.

549
00:44:25,497 --> 00:44:28,167
Dream of me as something good.

550
00:44:32,587 --> 00:44:36,217
<i>Don't despair, step right up
Glass of water, here's a cup</i>

551
00:44:36,675 --> 00:44:39,594
<i>Dream, dream, dream
Dream, dream, dream</i>

552
00:44:39,803 --> 00:44:42,348
He's having a nightmare.
Wake up, Max! Wake up!

553
00:44:42,556 --> 00:44:45,851
Stop that racket, Sharkboy.
You're giving him nightmares!

554
00:44:47,186 --> 00:44:48,895
Sorry, Max.

555
00:44:52,983 --> 00:44:55,652
-What was that for?
-Your nightmare was about me...

556
00:44:55,861 --> 00:44:57,447
...wasn't it?

557
00:44:58,322 --> 00:45:00,283
I don't remember.

558
00:45:00,824 --> 00:45:03,411
But I did dream about one thing.

559
00:45:04,037 --> 00:45:06,122
Plug Hounds!

560
00:45:08,540 --> 00:45:10,834
This may come as a shock to you.

561
00:45:14,130 --> 00:45:16,590
Feel the power!

562
00:45:21,011 --> 00:45:22,472
It's empty.

563
00:45:24,723 --> 00:45:26,517
Fudge.

564
00:45:26,725 --> 00:45:30,771
-I forgot to dream of gas.
-Max!

565
00:45:46,162 --> 00:45:48,164
My powers are weakening.

566
00:45:52,335 --> 00:45:55,962
Watch the power lines,
very dangerous.

567
00:46:28,246 --> 00:46:32,958
-Sharkboy, get me down from here!
-Can't you see I'm busy?

568
00:46:52,186 --> 00:46:55,148
Hot lava. Hot lava.

569
00:47:00,236 --> 00:47:03,989
-I don't got much fight left in me, Max.
-Where's Lavagirl?

570
00:47:06,074 --> 00:47:09,995
It's up to you now, Max.
Dream us out of here.

571
00:47:10,662 --> 00:47:12,831
We believe in you, Max.

572
00:47:14,916 --> 00:47:18,670
Shark Boat with turbo boosters.
Shark Boat with turbo boosters!

573
00:47:22,592 --> 00:47:24,510
A banana split?

574
00:47:24,718 --> 00:47:28,096
Still hungry, Max?
How about a knuckle sandwich?

575
00:47:28,306 --> 00:47:30,140
No, look.

576
00:47:31,016 --> 00:47:32,851
It's a banana split boat.

577
00:47:33,727 --> 00:47:34,978
Then let's split!

578
00:48:01,464 --> 00:48:03,424
Catch you later.

579
00:48:04,592 --> 00:48:08,512
All dreamers must dream.

580
00:48:09,930 --> 00:48:13,392
This is great, Max.
You're starting to daydream.

581
00:48:13,601 --> 00:48:16,811
Keep that up
and they'll never get us.

582
00:48:17,020 --> 00:48:18,564
Why not?

583
00:48:19,189 --> 00:48:21,359
Learn to dream
with your eyes open...

584
00:48:21,567 --> 00:48:23,902
...then you won't have to
be asleep to dream.

585
00:48:24,110 --> 00:48:27,906
You'll be able to make
anything happen at any time.

586
00:48:30,784 --> 00:48:33,787
<i>Row, row, row
Your banana split boat</i>

587
00:48:33,995 --> 00:48:36,582
<i>Gently down
The Stream of Consciousness</i>

588
00:48:36,790 --> 00:48:39,751
<i>Merrily, merrily, merrily, merrily
Life is Max's dream</i>

589
00:48:43,797 --> 00:48:45,549
Sugar will give you nightmares.

590
00:48:45,757 --> 00:48:48,552
-How much time do we have?
-Don't ask.

591
00:48:49,886 --> 00:48:52,138
The Dream Lair's across
the Ocean of Ice.

592
00:48:52,348 --> 00:48:55,225
We'll have to travel there by foot.

593
00:48:55,434 --> 00:48:57,936
What was it you saw
in your dream, Max?

594
00:48:59,062 --> 00:49:03,024
I saw an object shaped like....

595
00:49:03,775 --> 00:49:06,111
Give me something to draw with.

596
00:49:17,998 --> 00:49:19,791
The Crystal Heart.

597
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:24,588
That's the treasure of the
Land of Ice, in the Ice Castle.

598
00:49:24,796 --> 00:49:28,467
It can freeze anything, even time.

599
00:49:28,967 --> 00:49:31,803
I've always dreamt
of freezing a moment in time.

600
00:49:32,012 --> 00:49:34,598
And the Ice Castle's
ruled by the Ice Princess.

601
00:49:34,806 --> 00:49:37,560
I hear she's the most
beautiful girl on the planet.

602
00:49:39,019 --> 00:49:43,148
She is not! She's cold and cruel
and cares for nobody but herself.

603
00:49:43,357 --> 00:49:45,359
She's just saying that, Max.

604
00:49:45,568 --> 00:49:48,612
-You met her?
-No, but I know we don't get along.

605
00:49:48,820 --> 00:49:53,116
-How do you know that?
-I'm fire, she's ice.

606
00:49:53,326 --> 00:49:57,413
-We must be enemies.
-We need that Crystal Heart.

607
00:49:57,621 --> 00:50:00,040
But I need you both to get it.

608
00:50:01,166 --> 00:50:03,209
I just hope this isn't a trap.

609
00:50:08,256 --> 00:50:10,842
If we freeze time
with the Crystal Heart...

610
00:50:11,051 --> 00:50:14,430
...we'll be able to make it to
the Dream Lair and save the planet.

611
00:50:14,638 --> 00:50:16,682
That's the plan.

612
00:50:18,850 --> 00:50:23,814
Behold the Ice Castle. Home
to the princess of the Land of Ice.

613
00:50:24,022 --> 00:50:28,151
-The Crystal Heart's inside the castle?
-So they say.

614
00:50:28,361 --> 00:50:30,195
Let's go.

615
00:50:49,548 --> 00:50:52,385
It's no use. I'll melt the bridge.

616
00:50:52,593 --> 00:50:54,804
This place inflames me.

617
00:50:55,011 --> 00:50:57,263
Can you cool down enough
to get across?

618
00:50:57,473 --> 00:50:59,433
I'd have to be asleep to do that.

619
00:51:00,393 --> 00:51:02,645
Can you try sleepwalking?

620
00:51:07,775 --> 00:51:12,530
My dream is to live on Earth,
but someplace warm.

621
00:51:13,238 --> 00:51:17,576
And that Earth will accept me.
Even if I...

622
00:51:18,243 --> 00:51:22,080
...destroy everything I touch.

623
00:51:22,748 --> 00:51:27,377
No, Lavagirl! Don't sneeze!

624
00:51:42,852 --> 00:51:44,478
Look.

625
00:51:45,937 --> 00:51:47,690
She's sleeping.

626
00:52:06,459 --> 00:52:09,169
They found us again. Lavagirl!

627
00:52:09,837 --> 00:52:12,548
If you wake her up, she'll reheat.

628
00:52:13,298 --> 00:52:15,133
She can make it.

629
00:52:23,726 --> 00:52:26,186
Lavagirl, they're behind you!

630
00:52:46,874 --> 00:52:49,334
Let's go. Hurry!

631
00:52:51,712 --> 00:52:53,923
It's a trap!

632
00:52:54,840 --> 00:53:00,011
You can almost feel the
electricity in the air, can't you?

633
00:53:00,220 --> 00:53:04,642
This is all wrong.
Someone else's dreams are in here.

634
00:53:04,850 --> 00:53:07,101
Lights out.

635
00:53:19,447 --> 00:53:22,660
Welcome to the Dream Lair.

636
00:53:22,868 --> 00:53:25,704
I am the ruler of Planet Drool.

637
00:53:25,913 --> 00:53:29,249
No, you're not. Max is.

638
00:53:29,792 --> 00:53:33,253
Max may have
dreamed it originally...

639
00:53:35,923 --> 00:53:40,010
...but I made it much cooler.

640
00:53:40,218 --> 00:53:43,137
I am Minus.

641
00:53:44,682 --> 00:53:48,936
-How'd you get so powerful?
-I do a lot of reading.

642
00:53:49,143 --> 00:53:50,771
My book of dreams.

643
00:53:51,145 --> 00:53:55,025
That's why everything
is so messed up. He's changing it.

644
00:53:55,233 --> 00:53:57,653
Electric eels.

645
00:54:01,114 --> 00:54:03,951
Shocking, isn't it, Sharkboy?

646
00:54:04,158 --> 00:54:08,038
Reminds me of the time
that electrical storm...

647
00:54:08,246 --> 00:54:11,584
...blew apart your father's laboratory.

648
00:54:12,918 --> 00:54:16,504
-Where is my father?
-Let's see.

649
00:54:21,010 --> 00:54:22,928
Check the bottom of the ocean.

650
00:54:25,931 --> 00:54:28,266
And Lavagirl.

651
00:54:28,474 --> 00:54:31,311
Once I figure out
how to freeze this planet's core...

652
00:54:31,519 --> 00:54:33,897
...all of your powers will disappear.

653
00:54:34,105 --> 00:54:36,942
Powers? What powers?

654
00:54:39,485 --> 00:54:43,032
And last but least, Max.

655
00:54:43,239 --> 00:54:46,242
You thought you could escape fear
by running away to Dreamland...

656
00:54:46,451 --> 00:54:51,289
...but fear exists in the one place
you can never escape.

657
00:54:52,457 --> 00:54:54,459
Your mind.

658
00:54:55,878 --> 00:54:57,921
I will show you
the true meaning of fear.

659
00:54:58,171 --> 00:55:01,215
When Darkness falls, the rest
of your dreams will be destroyed...

660
00:55:01,424 --> 00:55:04,053
...and I will rule Planet Drool.

661
00:55:04,260 --> 00:55:05,553
Blah, blah, blah...

662
00:55:05,804 --> 00:55:07,681
...threat, threat, threat.

663
00:55:07,890 --> 00:55:12,352
You must all leave now.
I have some dreaming to do.

664
00:55:22,320 --> 00:55:24,990
If I could just get my dream journal...

665
00:55:26,407 --> 00:55:29,327
...I could turn everything back
to the way it was.

666
00:55:30,495 --> 00:55:32,622
My fire's dimming.

667
00:55:35,042 --> 00:55:39,672
-I can't melt the bars.
-My strength is failing me as well.

668
00:55:41,172 --> 00:55:43,216
How much time do we have,
Sharkboy?

669
00:55:43,717 --> 00:55:47,721
Who cares?
We're never getting out of here.

670
00:55:49,890 --> 00:55:51,975
La La's.

671
00:55:58,982 --> 00:56:00,316
They like you.

672
00:56:00,525 --> 00:56:03,737
-I don't feel destructive right now.
-I do!

673
00:56:03,946 --> 00:56:06,073
This song is driving me crazy.

674
00:56:06,489 --> 00:56:09,159
Don't worry about him.
He's a cold fish.

675
00:56:09,367 --> 00:56:11,536
I'm serious.

676
00:56:12,162 --> 00:56:15,040
They're singing at a frequency...

677
00:56:15,248 --> 00:56:19,335
...my highly trained ears
find disturbing!

678
00:56:19,544 --> 00:56:21,797
Sing louder. Sing higher.

679
00:56:25,926 --> 00:56:28,469
You don't want to be too close
to him when he explodes.

680
00:56:31,347 --> 00:56:32,850
Shark frenzy!

681
00:56:45,570 --> 00:56:47,906
Nice job channeling your anger,
Sharkie.

682
00:57:18,979 --> 00:57:22,690
First things first,
transportation out of here.

683
00:57:25,903 --> 00:57:27,863
My dreams.

684
00:57:31,867 --> 00:57:35,954
-Lavagirl, you have a Lava Bike.
-I do?

685
00:57:36,872 --> 00:57:38,581
I do!

686
00:57:41,417 --> 00:57:45,214
-This is so exciting.
-Cool it, Lavagirl.

687
00:57:45,421 --> 00:57:47,925
Everything we need
is right here in this book.

688
00:57:50,969 --> 00:57:52,637
Sharkboy...

689
00:57:53,679 --> 00:57:56,390
...your father really is
at the bottom of the ocean.

690
00:58:03,731 --> 00:58:05,984
He's in a submarine...

691
00:58:06,819 --> 00:58:08,821
...looking for you.

692
00:58:11,824 --> 00:58:14,784
He's over the hydrothermal vents,
Mid-Atlantic Ridge...

693
00:58:14,993 --> 00:58:17,120
...42 degrees west by 14 north.

694
00:58:17,328 --> 00:58:21,166
Depth, 1800 meters.
Near Snake Pit.

695
00:58:21,834 --> 00:58:25,170
-I need to get back to Earth.
-What's it say about me?

696
00:58:25,378 --> 00:58:28,381
-I'm not sure what this is.
-I can figure it out.

697
00:58:28,589 --> 00:58:30,633
Maybe there's a section
on my true identity.

698
00:58:30,843 --> 00:58:32,552
Lavagirl, no!

699
00:58:33,469 --> 00:58:35,013
Oh, no.

700
00:58:35,513 --> 00:58:39,142
-What have I done?
-That's terrific, LG.

701
00:58:42,603 --> 00:58:44,564
It's okay, Lavagirl.

702
00:58:44,772 --> 00:58:47,025
It was an accident.

703
00:58:47,234 --> 00:58:50,528
Why did you make me out of lava?
Why, Max?

704
00:58:52,114 --> 00:58:56,534
Just let her cool down.
She's just blowing off steam.

705
00:59:00,998 --> 00:59:03,333
I know I can be good.

706
00:59:04,209 --> 00:59:06,003
I can feel it.

707
00:59:07,670 --> 00:59:10,756
But everything I touch, I destroy.

708
00:59:11,841 --> 00:59:14,427
Why'd you make me like that?

709
00:59:15,345 --> 00:59:19,557
-I have more potential.
-I'm sure you do.

710
00:59:21,059 --> 00:59:25,272
Why'd you make us a team?
We're nothing alike.

711
00:59:25,479 --> 00:59:29,483
When I'm near water, I fizzle out.
When he's near heat, he shrivels.

712
00:59:29,692 --> 00:59:31,236
We're not compatible.

713
00:59:32,905 --> 00:59:35,908
Your hair's on fire.

714
00:59:36,116 --> 00:59:38,409
Yeah, it does that.

715
00:59:41,662 --> 00:59:43,248
Thanks, Sharkie.

716
00:59:46,376 --> 00:59:48,711
Maybe I really am evil.

717
00:59:49,503 --> 00:59:53,175
So far everything else
you've dreamed has been correct.

718
00:59:54,217 --> 00:59:56,761
Maybe I just need
to learn to accept it.

719
00:59:58,221 --> 01:00:02,433
That's it. Everything I've
dreamt so far has been correct.

720
01:00:02,642 --> 01:00:04,144
The Crystal Heart.

721
01:00:04,353 --> 01:00:05,895
Yeah, we were captured...

722
01:00:06,104 --> 01:00:09,066
...but that's because Minus
doesn't want me to get it.

723
01:00:13,819 --> 01:00:16,114
We have to get back
to the Ice Castle.

724
01:00:16,323 --> 01:00:18,866
Ten minutes left.
We'll never make it.

725
01:00:19,076 --> 01:00:20,826
We can do it!

726
01:00:21,036 --> 01:00:22,412
-How?
-How?

727
01:00:22,620 --> 01:00:26,540
You're Sharkboy and Lavagirl.
You can do anything.

728
01:00:34,132 --> 01:00:35,883
Wake up.

729
01:00:37,593 --> 01:00:40,222
-What?
-He escaped.

730
01:00:40,430 --> 01:00:42,515
He's getting the Crystal Heart.

731
01:00:42,723 --> 01:00:45,518
-Shut it down. Shut it all down now.
-I did!

732
01:00:45,726 --> 01:00:49,231
It's on a grid system. It takes time
for the Darkness to travel.

733
01:00:49,439 --> 01:00:51,774
-How soon?
-Not soon enough.

734
01:00:51,984 --> 01:00:54,361
-Then destroy him.
-How?

735
01:00:54,568 --> 01:00:57,571
By smashing
his most precious dream:

736
01:00:58,031 --> 01:01:00,700
Sharkboy and Lavagirl.

737
01:01:20,511 --> 01:01:24,016
-Is that what you saw, Max?
-Yes.

738
01:01:24,224 --> 01:01:27,019
You'll have to climb
the ice pillar and get it.

739
01:01:27,560 --> 01:01:31,314
It's as delicate as a snowflake,
so don't drop it.

740
01:01:31,522 --> 01:01:36,278
Don't touch it with your hands either.
You'll freeze! Use your claws.

741
01:01:51,460 --> 01:01:53,586
Lava, can you--?

742
01:01:54,212 --> 01:01:55,963
Never mind.

743
01:01:57,006 --> 01:02:00,218
Chew on some ice.
It'll keep you cool.

744
01:02:32,459 --> 01:02:34,710
Great job, Max!

745
01:02:40,007 --> 01:02:41,842
I got it!

746
01:02:48,766 --> 01:02:50,601
She's frozen solid!

747
01:03:09,036 --> 01:03:11,622
Kneel before the Ice Princess.

748
01:03:21,424 --> 01:03:24,927
You tried to steal
the Crystal Heart. Why?

749
01:03:28,431 --> 01:03:30,683
We believe it can freeze time.

750
01:03:30,891 --> 01:03:33,102
Long enough for us to defeat Minus.

751
01:03:33,311 --> 01:03:37,773
My Crystal Heart cannot help you.
Only I have the power to use it.

752
01:03:37,982 --> 01:03:40,943
-Then come with us.
-She can never leave this castle.

753
01:03:41,153 --> 01:03:46,616
The Crystal is the only thing
that protects our kingdom.

754
01:03:46,824 --> 01:03:49,327
Please, princess,
we're running out of time.

755
01:03:49,536 --> 01:03:53,206
-Perhaps I could give it to you.
-Not without my blessing.

756
01:03:53,415 --> 01:03:55,542
Father, you're smothering me again.

757
01:03:56,917 --> 01:04:00,338
-But are you worthy to wield it?
-Yes.

758
01:04:00,754 --> 01:04:03,216
The crystal you stole was a decoy.

759
01:04:03,425 --> 01:04:06,886
The true Crystal Heart
is somewhere in this room.

760
01:04:07,094 --> 01:04:10,848
Choose the correct one
and you may carry it before you.

761
01:04:11,391 --> 01:04:12,850
Pick that one.

762
01:04:15,187 --> 01:04:17,021
It's around your neck.

763
01:04:19,524 --> 01:04:22,611
-How did you know?
-I saw it in my dream.

764
01:04:23,777 --> 01:04:26,113
Usually if you snooze, you lose.

765
01:04:26,323 --> 01:04:29,326
With Max, you snooze, you win.

766
01:04:33,371 --> 01:04:37,542
But be warned, Max, if anything
happens to my Crystal Heart...

767
01:04:38,210 --> 01:04:41,254
...my entire kingdom
will be destroyed.

768
01:04:41,463 --> 01:04:44,006
Do you, Max,
take this Crystal Heart...

769
01:04:44,216 --> 01:04:47,009
...to have and to hold,
in sickness and in health...

770
01:04:47,219 --> 01:04:50,012
-...till death do you part?
-I do.

771
01:04:50,222 --> 01:04:52,599
-Do you trust him with your heart?
-I do.

772
01:04:52,806 --> 01:04:55,059
Do you mean what you say?

773
01:04:55,726 --> 01:04:58,812
Yes. I mean, I do.

774
01:04:59,021 --> 01:05:02,900
The Crystal will now work,
but my daughter must stay here.

775
01:05:03,108 --> 01:05:06,655
-Off with you then.
-Good luck.

776
01:05:14,161 --> 01:05:16,956
We're almost to the Dream Lair.

777
01:05:17,164 --> 01:05:20,252
If we're gonna do this,
we gotta do it now.

778
01:05:20,460 --> 01:05:24,129
-How much time?
-We're out of time.

779
01:05:24,339 --> 01:05:26,131
Ten seconds.

780
01:05:33,598 --> 01:05:36,141
What? I can't hear you.

781
01:05:36,351 --> 01:05:38,561
-Five seconds.
-Here it goes.

782
01:05:38,769 --> 01:05:41,939
Three, two, one.

783
01:05:44,567 --> 01:05:47,069
-We're out of time.
-What happened?

784
01:05:47,279 --> 01:05:50,864
-It didn't work.
-How could it not work?

785
01:05:53,576 --> 01:05:55,662
I was trying to tell you.

786
01:05:57,497 --> 01:05:59,457
Only the Ice Princess can use it.

787
01:05:59,666 --> 01:06:02,585
It's not her fault her father
won't let her leave her castle.

788
01:06:02,793 --> 01:06:04,296
Boo-hoo!

789
01:06:04,671 --> 01:06:07,006
No underwater readings.

790
01:06:08,132 --> 01:06:10,217
No anything.

791
01:06:17,141 --> 01:06:20,185
I'll rip his circuits to shreds!

792
01:06:20,395 --> 01:06:23,523
Calm down, Sharkboy.
Mr. Electric's baiting you.

793
01:06:24,649 --> 01:06:30,029
-I can't fight my instincts!
-No, Sharkboy!

794
01:06:35,034 --> 01:06:36,494
Hey!

795
01:06:36,827 --> 01:06:39,163
"Watts" up?

796
01:06:39,913 --> 01:06:41,708
You know, "watts."

797
01:06:42,166 --> 01:06:44,794
As in a measure of electrical power.

798
01:06:45,252 --> 01:06:47,339
The 60-watt bulb?

799
01:06:47,672 --> 01:06:50,425
Watts up?

800
01:06:51,300 --> 01:06:52,510
Watt?

801
01:06:52,719 --> 01:06:54,970
Electric eels.

802
01:06:55,179 --> 01:06:56,806
That's what's up.

803
01:06:57,014 --> 01:06:59,351
Swim away, Sharkboy!
Swim away!

804
01:07:19,953 --> 01:07:22,081
Can he survive down there?

805
01:07:22,289 --> 01:07:25,334
He can hold his breath,
but not forever.

806
01:07:25,543 --> 01:07:29,464
-He'll drown if I don't go get him.
-I can't let you go.

807
01:07:29,880 --> 01:07:31,924
You'll die too.

808
01:07:34,218 --> 01:07:36,388
He's my best friend.

809
01:07:58,951 --> 01:08:01,203
Come on, Sharkboy.

810
01:08:08,043 --> 01:08:10,003
Come on, Sharkboy.

811
01:08:17,595 --> 01:08:20,139
Sharkboy. Wake up, Sharkboy.

812
01:08:25,144 --> 01:08:26,395
Lavagirl!

813
01:08:27,312 --> 01:08:30,859
Lavagirl! Lavagirl, please.

814
01:08:31,400 --> 01:08:33,277
Lavagirl.

815
01:08:39,158 --> 01:08:41,243
What am I gonna do now?

816
01:08:43,370 --> 01:08:46,833
What do you think you should do?

817
01:08:48,333 --> 01:08:50,377
Dream a better dream?

818
01:08:50,587 --> 01:08:53,840
Interesting. Explain.

819
01:08:54,466 --> 01:08:57,384
I wanted all my dreams
to come true...

820
01:08:57,677 --> 01:08:59,970
...but I only dreamt for myself.

821
01:09:00,345 --> 01:09:02,973
I wanted to escape my real world...

822
01:09:03,182 --> 01:09:06,895
...when the world needed my help
to make it a better place.

823
01:09:08,480 --> 01:09:11,273
Selfish dreams shouldn't come true.

824
01:09:11,483 --> 01:09:14,569
You're becoming
a very good dreamer, Max.

825
01:09:14,777 --> 01:09:17,655
A very good dreamer indeed.

826
01:09:19,323 --> 01:09:21,283
What do you do...

827
01:09:21,493 --> 01:09:23,953
...when your dreams
have been destroyed?

828
01:09:24,161 --> 01:09:26,789
Dream a better dream.

829
01:09:26,997 --> 01:09:30,668
An unselfish dream.

830
01:09:37,466 --> 01:09:39,886
She knew this would happen
if she saved you.

831
01:09:40,678 --> 01:09:42,847
I couldn't stop her.

832
01:09:46,809 --> 01:09:48,143
Look.

833
01:09:50,563 --> 01:09:51,856
Lava.

834
01:09:54,066 --> 01:09:56,986
-We have to get her to that volcano.
-I'll go.

835
01:09:57,194 --> 01:10:00,573
-I'm stronger and faster.
-You'll burn up.

836
01:10:04,326 --> 01:10:08,205
-Are you sure this will save her?
-It'll do more than save her.

837
01:10:15,420 --> 01:10:18,298
I know who you are, Lavagirl.

838
01:10:19,299 --> 01:10:23,512
You are not fire, or a simple flame.

839
01:10:23,721 --> 01:10:26,056
You are greater than that.

840
01:10:26,558 --> 01:10:28,851
Something more important.

841
01:10:29,059 --> 01:10:31,436
And so necessary.

842
01:10:31,729 --> 01:10:34,314
It is why you must live.

843
01:10:38,193 --> 01:10:40,320
You are not destruction.

844
01:10:49,664 --> 01:10:51,331
You are not evil.

845
01:11:01,634 --> 01:11:02,969
Stand back.

846
01:11:05,345 --> 01:11:06,598
You are...

847
01:11:06,806 --> 01:11:08,181
...light.

848
01:11:21,738 --> 01:11:24,699
Who turned on the lights?

849
01:11:26,450 --> 01:11:29,078
Power! Everywhere!

850
01:11:45,762 --> 01:11:47,262
How did you get here so fast?

851
01:11:47,471 --> 01:11:50,642
Hold off Mr. Electric
while I deal with Minus.

852
01:11:50,850 --> 01:11:53,102
I'll need my fish army.

853
01:11:53,435 --> 01:11:55,270
I'll unfreeze the ocean.

854
01:11:57,439 --> 01:11:58,941
Good luck.

855
01:12:02,569 --> 01:12:06,281
I've become what
you feared most, Minus.

856
01:12:08,200 --> 01:12:11,370
-How did you get in here?
-I'm the Daydreamer.

857
01:12:11,578 --> 01:12:15,624
Able to dream with my eyes open.

858
01:12:15,833 --> 01:12:19,336
Hate to burst your bubble,
dream boy, but I read your book.

859
01:12:19,544 --> 01:12:23,507
There's not one dream you've got
that I haven't already seen.

860
01:12:23,716 --> 01:12:25,467
So, what do you say?

861
01:12:25,677 --> 01:12:28,930
Let's blow the roof off this place.

862
01:12:33,101 --> 01:12:35,853
May the best dream win.

863
01:13:00,128 --> 01:13:02,004
Wait.

864
01:13:06,550 --> 01:13:08,301
Brainstorm.

865
01:13:24,068 --> 01:13:25,444
Brain...

866
01:13:25,652 --> 01:13:27,362
...freeze!

867
01:13:30,032 --> 01:13:32,118
Brain...

868
01:13:32,910 --> 01:13:34,162
...fart.

869
01:13:54,932 --> 01:13:57,559
Get ready for the
ultimate power outage.

870
01:13:59,561 --> 01:14:04,817
And who are you to believe
that you can defeat me now?

871
01:14:05,358 --> 01:14:06,903
No one special.

872
01:14:07,111 --> 01:14:08,695
Just...

873
01:14:09,613 --> 01:14:10,907
...King of the Ocean.

874
01:14:24,628 --> 01:14:26,713
Shark frenzy.

875
01:14:32,302 --> 01:14:34,180
You're afraid of me, aren't you?

876
01:14:39,351 --> 01:14:40,727
I used to be.

877
01:14:44,941 --> 01:14:46,943
Someone smashed
your dreams once.

878
01:14:47,151 --> 01:14:50,112
Now all you can do
is smash everyone else's.

879
01:14:58,453 --> 01:15:01,123
We can create
a better dream than this.

880
01:15:01,331 --> 01:15:04,668
A better world. Don't you see?

881
01:15:10,799 --> 01:15:12,384
What do you say...

882
01:15:13,845 --> 01:15:15,470
...Linus?

883
01:15:27,649 --> 01:15:29,193
Hurry.

884
01:15:35,908 --> 01:15:39,661
Don't let me fall!

885
01:15:41,538 --> 01:15:42,999
Wouldn't dream of it.

886
01:15:52,382 --> 01:15:54,551
Don't smash
people's dreams, Linus...

887
01:15:54,759 --> 01:15:56,845
...because you'll smash
your own as well.

888
01:15:57,470 --> 01:15:59,598
And you too will stop believing.

889
01:16:04,061 --> 01:16:05,729
Max.

890
01:16:06,230 --> 01:16:08,149
I am light.

891
01:16:08,357 --> 01:16:11,319
-Thank you.
-You were always that.

892
01:16:11,526 --> 01:16:13,528
Had nothing to do with me.

893
01:16:13,737 --> 01:16:14,989
But now I know.

894
01:16:15,197 --> 01:16:16,781
So thank you.

895
01:16:16,991 --> 01:16:19,534
Okay, so she's a light.

896
01:16:19,743 --> 01:16:21,203
Big deal.

897
01:16:21,411 --> 01:16:23,039
The real news is...

898
01:16:23,788 --> 01:16:25,582
...what I am.

899
01:16:25,832 --> 01:16:28,044
Annoying?

900
01:16:28,752 --> 01:16:30,462
King of the Ocean.

901
01:16:31,255 --> 01:16:33,090
Thanks for saving me.

902
01:16:37,427 --> 01:16:38,930
Ouch.

903
01:16:39,471 --> 01:16:42,183
Everything will return
to being the way it was.

904
01:16:42,391 --> 01:16:45,394
You will be able to travel to Earth
and back again as you wish.

905
01:16:45,602 --> 01:16:48,940
You can search for your father.
You can rule Earth's lava world.

906
01:16:49,315 --> 01:16:53,945
And what am I to do,
now that you're all buddy-buddy?

907
01:16:54,819 --> 01:16:58,032
Mr. Electric can go back to being
the good electrician of the planet.

908
01:17:00,117 --> 01:17:03,578
Oh, really?
Plugging in power cords?

909
01:17:03,787 --> 01:17:07,416
Keeping this loud,
obnoxious world a happy place?

910
01:17:07,624 --> 01:17:10,336
-You're dreaming.
-I dreamt you up...

911
01:17:10,543 --> 01:17:13,255
-...and I can undream you.
-You think you can just...

912
01:17:13,463 --> 01:17:17,550
...snap your eyes open and
make me vanish? Not so easy.

913
01:17:17,759 --> 01:17:20,429
I am the danger of dreaming.

914
01:17:20,720 --> 01:17:23,391
For every person who dreams up
the electric light bulb...

915
01:17:23,598 --> 01:17:26,978
...there's the one who
dreams up the atom bomb.

916
01:17:27,186 --> 01:17:29,479
This is one dream
you won't be waking up from.

917
01:17:29,688 --> 01:17:33,858
I'm gonna put an end to this
ridiculous tangent at its source.

918
01:17:35,987 --> 01:17:37,238
Where did he go?

919
01:17:39,656 --> 01:17:41,075
He's headed to Earth.

920
01:17:41,325 --> 01:17:44,619
He's going to try
and destroy you in your sleep.

921
01:17:45,745 --> 01:17:47,664
In my sleep?

922
01:17:49,624 --> 01:17:51,835
You mean I'm asleep?

923
01:17:52,669 --> 01:17:55,630
-All this time I've been asleep?
-No.

924
01:17:55,839 --> 01:17:57,716
You're dreaming, Max.

925
01:17:57,924 --> 01:18:01,720
-With your eyes open.
-Make the dream real.

926
01:18:01,928 --> 01:18:04,181
You can live out
your dreams on Earth.

927
01:18:04,390 --> 01:18:06,434
Just like you made us real.

928
01:18:06,641 --> 01:18:11,063
-Make it real.
-Blink your eyes three times.

929
01:18:11,272 --> 01:18:13,149
One.

930
01:18:13,357 --> 01:18:15,692
Wait. What happens when--?

931
01:18:15,900 --> 01:18:17,902
Two.

932
01:18:19,447 --> 01:18:21,365
Will I ever see you again?

933
01:18:21,573 --> 01:18:23,034
Three.

934
01:18:30,999 --> 01:18:32,876
Everyone follow me!

935
01:18:33,085 --> 01:18:35,379
We gotta find shelter!

936
01:18:36,004 --> 01:18:37,797
Max, get up!

937
01:18:38,006 --> 01:18:40,675
There's a tornado heading our way!

938
01:18:42,219 --> 01:18:44,388
It's not a tornado!

939
01:18:45,306 --> 01:18:47,557
It's much worse than that!

940
01:18:47,766 --> 01:18:50,018
Linus, wake up!

941
01:18:50,227 --> 01:18:51,936
Look!

942
01:19:00,237 --> 01:19:02,406
Charge!

943
01:19:02,614 --> 01:19:05,242
It's Mr. Electric from Planet Drool!

944
01:19:05,451 --> 01:19:07,702
The one from my dreams!

945
01:19:07,911 --> 01:19:10,206
You mean this is real?

946
01:19:10,414 --> 01:19:12,040
Your dream is real?

947
01:19:12,458 --> 01:19:15,919
Some dreams are so powerful
they become real.

948
01:19:16,378 --> 01:19:17,754
I don't believe it.

949
01:19:17,962 --> 01:19:20,424
-It's right there in front of you!
-I can see that.

950
01:19:20,632 --> 01:19:22,426
What I can't believe is...

951
01:19:22,634 --> 01:19:25,637
...you dreamt me
as a big round bad guy.

952
01:19:25,845 --> 01:19:27,098
I'm not bad.

953
01:19:27,556 --> 01:19:31,143
Sorry. It kind of took on
a life of its own.

954
01:19:35,772 --> 01:19:40,569
-Max is in building C.
-No, he's not, he's in building W.

955
01:19:40,777 --> 01:19:43,322
That was the other school.

956
01:20:01,923 --> 01:20:04,759
Find Max.
Tell him I love him.

957
01:20:04,968 --> 01:20:08,472
-Don't leave me.
-I thought you wanted me to leave.

958
01:20:08,721 --> 01:20:12,476
No, I don't.
You're my best friend.

959
01:20:13,059 --> 01:20:14,853
I love you.

960
01:20:15,979 --> 01:20:17,523
I love you too.

961
01:20:22,486 --> 01:20:24,488
Come back!

962
01:20:26,157 --> 01:20:29,160
Please, come back.

963
01:20:38,042 --> 01:20:40,171
I'm not going anywhere.

964
01:20:41,671 --> 01:20:43,798
Neither am I.

965
01:21:03,485 --> 01:21:05,737
Okay, class, I'm just a teacher...

966
01:21:05,945 --> 01:21:08,324
...and I'm here to inspire
the answers from you.

967
01:21:08,532 --> 01:21:11,117
And I think that's some
pretty good inspiration outside.

968
01:21:11,327 --> 01:21:13,077
So this is now a pop quiz.

969
01:21:13,287 --> 01:21:14,954
We need to defeat that guy.

970
01:21:15,623 --> 01:21:17,707
Any ideas?

971
01:21:18,250 --> 01:21:21,212
Wow, Linus, you get a plus
for being the first hand in the air.

972
01:21:21,420 --> 01:21:23,255
I can take him.

973
01:21:23,755 --> 01:21:25,257
Linus, watch out!

974
01:21:36,644 --> 01:21:37,936
Nice try.

975
01:21:38,144 --> 01:21:39,480
Sorry, Max.

976
01:21:39,688 --> 01:21:42,316
-Your journal.
-It's okay.

977
01:21:42,524 --> 01:21:46,237
It was an accident. Plenty more
dreams where those came from.

978
01:21:47,904 --> 01:21:51,199
Okay, kids, who's next?
Remember, there are no dumb ideas.

979
01:21:51,408 --> 01:21:53,034
Maybe we can freeze his circuits.

980
01:21:53,244 --> 01:21:54,786
That's the dumbest idea
I've ever heard.

981
01:21:54,994 --> 01:21:56,746
We're in the middle
of Texas in August.

982
01:21:56,955 --> 01:22:00,124
-Next idea. Please, anyone but Linus.
-Wait, that's a great idea.

983
01:22:00,542 --> 01:22:01,918
Thanks, Linus.

984
01:22:02,253 --> 01:22:04,087
Come here, Marissa.

985
01:22:09,092 --> 01:22:10,969
Is this yours?

986
01:22:11,428 --> 01:22:12,929
How'd you find it?

987
01:22:13,430 --> 01:22:15,307
So you've seen this?

988
01:22:16,015 --> 01:22:19,936
Yes, but only in a dream.

989
01:22:20,144 --> 01:22:22,230
It can freeze anything.

990
01:22:22,439 --> 01:22:24,941
-Even time.
-What are you doing?

991
01:22:25,191 --> 01:22:26,985
You're not sending
my daughter out there.

992
01:22:27,193 --> 01:22:28,445
Let her out.

993
01:22:29,028 --> 01:22:32,616
Electrical storm, headed your way.

994
01:22:32,907 --> 01:22:36,244
-Do you know what to do?
-I believe so.

995
01:22:36,786 --> 01:22:38,622
Stand back.

996
01:22:46,129 --> 01:22:48,507
Well, what do we have here?

997
01:22:51,843 --> 01:22:55,472
Get ready for the "megahertz."

998
01:22:56,682 --> 01:22:59,560
-Get it? Hertz?
-Mega what?

999
01:22:59,976 --> 01:23:02,479
As in the unit
of electrical frequency?

1000
01:23:06,650 --> 01:23:09,861
Wow, you just aren't paying
attention in class, are you?

1001
01:23:21,831 --> 01:23:24,000
He's unplugged.

1002
01:23:32,426 --> 01:23:33,677
It's snowing out!

1003
01:23:41,059 --> 01:23:42,935
You made me a great teacher today.

1004
01:23:43,479 --> 01:23:44,813
How did I do that?

1005
01:23:45,021 --> 01:23:47,441
A great teacher learns as much
from his students...

1006
01:23:47,649 --> 01:23:48,776
...as they do from him.

1007
01:23:48,983 --> 01:23:50,985
You have...

1008
01:23:51,362 --> 01:23:53,237
...awakened me.

1009
01:23:53,863 --> 01:23:55,491
Thank you, Max.

1010
01:24:23,142 --> 01:24:24,686
Max...

1011
01:24:25,228 --> 01:24:27,481
...your report, please.

1012
01:24:36,615 --> 01:24:39,200
The following story is true.

1013
01:24:40,201 --> 01:24:42,328
It might have started as a dream.

1014
01:24:42,538 --> 01:24:43,913
But as we saw yesterday...

1015
01:24:45,373 --> 01:24:47,543
...when we make
our dreams a reality...

1016
01:24:47,751 --> 01:24:51,463
...reality becomes a dream.

1017
01:24:51,755 --> 01:24:54,550
<i>Sharkboy lives his dream
as King of the Ocean...</i>

1018
01:24:54,758 --> 01:24:57,678
<i>...where he cares
for all its creatures.</i>

1019
01:24:57,886 --> 01:25:01,890
<i>He searches for his father's
submarine where there is no light...</i>

1020
01:25:02,098 --> 01:25:04,183
<i>...except in one place...</i>

1021
01:25:04,392 --> 01:25:07,729
<i>...where light shines
almost as bright as the sun.</i>

1022
01:25:07,937 --> 01:25:10,231
<i>It's where Lavagirl
lives her dream...</i>

1023
01:25:10,441 --> 01:25:14,944
<i>...as queen of Earth's volcanoes
that boil at the bottom of the sea.</i>

1024
01:25:15,153 --> 01:25:17,781
<i>A force of life for all living things.</i>

1025
01:25:19,450 --> 01:25:22,536
<i>Sharkboy and Lavagirl
don't visit me anymore.</i>

1026
01:25:24,996 --> 01:25:29,125
<i>But I can visit them, in my dreams.</i>

1027
01:25:30,126 --> 01:25:32,880
<i>So dream a better dream...</i>

1028
01:25:33,672 --> 01:25:36,508
<i>...then work to make it real.</i>

1029
01:25:37,383 --> 01:25:39,177
<i>Yes?</i>

